1 SUBM @SUBM1@
1 NOTE This Gedcom file should only be used as part of the testsuite
2 CONT for Gedcom.pm (http://www.pjcj.net).  I have removed a
2 CONT lot of data from the original, and changed a few bits, so you
2 CONT should use the original if you want royal genealogy.  Contact me
2 CONT if you cannot locate the original.
2 CONT
2 CONT Paul Johnson (paul@pjcj.net)
2 CONT
2 CONT >> In a message to Cliff Manis (cmanis@csoftec.csf.com)
2 CONT >> Denis Reid wrote the following:
2 CONT >> Date: Fri, 25 Dec 92 14:12:32 -0500
2 CONT >> From: ah189@cleveland.Freenet.Edu (Denis Reid)
2 CONT >> Subject: THE ROYALS
2 CONT >> First of all,  MERRY CHRISTMAS!
2 CONT >>
2 CONT >> You may make this Royal GEDCOM available available to whomever.
2 CONT >> As you know this is a work in process and have received
2 CONT >> suggestions, corrections and additions from all over the planet...
2 CONT >> some even who claim to be descended from Charlemange, himself!
2 CONT >>
2 CONT >> The weakest part of the Royals is in the French and Spanish lines.
2 CONT >> I found that many of the French Kings had multiple mistresses
2 CONT >> whose descendants claimed noble titles, and the Throne itself in
2 CONT >> some cases.  I have had the hardest time finding good published
2 CONT >> sources for French and Spanish Royalty.
2 CONT >>
2 CONT >> If you do post it to a BBS or send it around, I would appreciate
2 CONT >> it if you'd append a message to the effect that I would welcome
2 CONT >> comments and suggestions and possible sources to improve the
2 CONT >> database.
2 CONT >>
2 CONT >> Since the Royals had so many names and many titles it was
2 CONT >> difficult to "fill in the blanks" with their name.  In the
2 CONT >> previous version, I included all their titles, names, monikers in
2 CONT >> the notes.
2 CONT >>
2 CONT >> Thanks for your interest.   Denis Reid
0 @SUBM1@ SUBM
